  "artDirection": "Same selected warm-tan child scientist with thoughtful amber eyes, fine brown clear round glasses, white bob/cat-ear headband, red scarf, white lab coat, dark clothes/boots/teal pouch. Soft dimensional game illustration. Scene1 rear chalkboard-writing professor, white headband ear backs, cat anatomy = liquid beaker and liquid??. Scene2 flask mixing, cream cat hanging supported from bookshelf, orange window-squeeze cat, pale-blue/green cats resting inside foreground glass containers; corrected small paws and coherent folded legs. Scene3 sudden explosion and diagonal feet-first suction into dark floor vortex, cream ledge cat has modest foreleg and thin tapered tail; rear leg now extends down-left with distinct knee, meaningful shin, ankle and smaller boot; near leg down-right; original upper body and front boot preserved. Scene4 scientist splashes into a clear turquoise woodland stream while resident green/orange/blue cats already float calmly BELLY UP like the lobby, with actual lobby-model-like long smooth fairly constant-width torsos, tiny chest forepaws and two short hindlegs extending along body axis with gap, no big upturned soles or banana tails; no laboratory containers; horizontal fading arrival portal on background rock ledge. Scene5 continues IN THE SAME STREAM: scientist wades waist-deep supporting green cat under upper chest with both hands; its surprisingly long relaxed torso hangs down and visibly continues in a gentle curve underwater; curious surprised scientist and drowsy cat. Orange/blue float nearby with same lobby-like shape. No glass vessels, dry paving, notebook in hands or measuring/pulling experiment. Scene6 green floor aperture reveals human cat playroom with cat tower/toys; the three FOREST cats look eagerly into it with wide round sparkling turquoise eyes and happy little smiles. Scenes7/8 color-portal guidance/farewell. Cats have rounded bodies, two forelegs from shoulders/two hindlegs from pelvis/one tapering tail, modest head-relative paw size; no inflated bear feet or tail resembling extra limb. Usually relaxed lazy eyes; scene6 discovery is the explicit exception with wide delighted eyes. No nasal sleep bubbles. Portals always horizontal. Revision18: scene1 vessel cats have continuous chest and modest paws at floor; scene3 background cats rest on ledges with small forepaws and ONE slender tail curled on ledge, no dangling sausage appendages. Forest orange cat in scenes4/5 is solid orange including muzzle/chest/feet/tail; no stripes/white patches, matching scenes6/7/8. Human-laboratory tabby cats and human playroom cats keep their own coat patterns. All eight angled comic rims are black (#111111).",
